## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-tenant isolation, data residency, idempotency, observability, and cost-conscious design in a fintech data-bridge.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub per-tenant isolation
- Dataflow streaming with dedupe
- BigQuery per-tenant datasets with partitioning
- IAM least privilege and per-tenant service accounts
- Data residency and cost controls
- Observability with Cloud Logging/Monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow-like transform
function process(event) {
  if (!event || !event.id) return;
  if (!seen.has(event.id)) {
    writeBigQuery(event);
    seen.add(event.id);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant isolation at scale?
- How would you handle late-arriving data and replays?
- What are your rollback/disaster-recovery considerations?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses practical ability to design region-specific, tenant-isolated data pipelines with proper security, onboarding, and DR considerations.

## Key Concepts

- Regional data residency per tenant
- Streaming ETL with Dataflow
- Idempotency and deduplication
- Tenant lifecycle automation (onboard/offboard)
- Security: CMEK, IAM least privilege
- Observability with Cloud Monitoring/Logging
- Disaster recovery and cost controls

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo dedup write to BigQuery per tenant
function writeEvent(evt) {
  const key = evt.tenantId + "_" + evt.eventId;
  if (dedupStore.has(key)) return;
  dedupStore.add(key);
  bigQueryWrite(evt);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate idempotency and replay safety in the Dataflow pipeline at scale?
- What would your DR test plan look like for region failover and data residency?
